  "narrative": "Scope: 212 storage events (cookies, localStorage, sessionStorage; no IndexedDB) plus 19 window property events, for a total of 231 events. One origin observed: https://www.premierleague.com. TRACE VALUE was searched across network, storage, and window properties and does not appear anywhere in this capture, so no specific origin trace is possible for that string.\n\nAuth & token patterns:\n- Primary auth appears to be handled via IAS/WSC tokens stored in localStorage:\n  - wsc_ias_accessToken is a full JWT access token with HS256 header and rich user claims (UserId, ExternalId, IsAnonymous, timestamps, issuer=WSC). This is the main credential likely sent on authenticated API calls.\n  - wsc_ias_refreshToken is a separate JWT refresh token with a longer expiry and minimal payload (no profile claims), used to mint new access tokens.\n  - Both tokens are written once in this capture and not refreshed, suggesting a relatively short session or that refresh was not triggered during the recorded period.\n- No CSRF/XSRF tokens or API keys (e.g., sk_live_, pk_) were observed in storage or window properties.\n- Several other identifiers behave like session or analytics tokens rather than auth:\n  - optimizely_data$$...$$session_state holds a UUID sessionId plus lastSessionTimestamp; updated multiple times as the Optimizely SDK records activity.\n  - tt_sessionId and tt_pixel_session_index are TikTok pixel session identifiers and counters (analytics only).\n  - sentryReplaySession is Sentry\u2019s own session token used for replay tracing, not for user auth.\n\nData caching & config:\n- Optimizely stores substantial structured data in localStorage under multiple keys:\n  - tracker_optimizely: a full event-batch payload including visitor attributes (logged_in flag, device, browser, source_type) and client_activation event details. This mirrors what is POSTed to Optimizely\u2019s logging endpoint.\n  - visitor_profile: a profile object keyed by visitorId with custom attributes and metadata.lastModified timestamps, effectively a local profile cache for experimentation and targeting.\n  - pending_events: a queue of one or more event batches waiting to be sent or retried, including campaign_activated and client_activation events.\n  - session_state: small but important state for Optimizely\u2019s session concept (UUID sessionId + lastSessionTimestamp), updated as the session progresses.\n- Sentry stores a compact JSON blob in sessionStorage (sentryReplaySession) tracking replay session id, timestamps, and sampling mode. This is configuration/state for error replay capture.\n- TikTok pixel uses sessionStorage for structured state in tt_pixel_session_index and a compound sessionId string in tt_sessionId.\n\nNoise & tracking:\n- A large proportion of storage keys are analytics/experimentation/consent related (Optimizely, Chartbeat, _cb*, _gcl_ls, Sentry, Adobe, OneTrust, tt_*). An approximate noise count from key pattern analysis is 151 events out of 231 total, which includes repeated updates to the same keys.\n- Many other keys represent UI preferences or feature flags (ff_* keys such as ff_copilot_refresh_prompts, ff_player_comparison, ff_fantasy, theme, appMaintenance*), which are important for UX but not security-sensitive tokens.\n\nWindow properties:\n- 19 window property events with 5569 unique paths were recorded, but no JWT-like strings, obvious API keys, or access/refresh/CSRF token values were found when searching for TRACE VALUE or when reviewing token-related storage keys. The sensitive auth material (WSC IAS tokens) is kept in localStorage rather than directly exposed on window.\n\nLifecycle & behavior:\n- On initial page load, Optimizely writes tracker_optimizely, visitor_profile, session_state, and later pending_events as it queues event batches. session_state is updated multiple times as activity timestamps change.\n- IAS/WSC tokens (accessToken and refreshToken) are written once early in the session and remain s